# {{PROJECT}} · Directory ownership

> **Only change directories you own.** For cross-directory work, write `BLOCKED:` in your report naming who should
> change what, and hand it back to the PM. Anything not listed here belongs to the PM.

| Path | Owner | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `<path>/**` | agent:<name> | <what this directory is responsible for> |
| `docs/**` | PM | Briefs / reports / verification / decisions. Narrow review exception: only `team review` may write the brief-named `docs/team/reviews/<ID>.md` and `<ID>-verify.log` in the main checkout; the verifier's own report stays on its task branch, and no other manual main-checkout write is granted |
| `.pi/**`, `AGENTS.md` | PM | Team protocol and configuration |
| `scripts/team*`, root config (lockfile/tsconfig, ...) | PM | New dependencies → raise them in the report |

## Roster

| Agent | Long-lived worktree | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| <name> | `.worktrees/<name>` | <module> |

> A seat is a roster name and a directory, **not a model**. Models are the project's task-category policy
> (`TEAM_TASK_MODELS` in `.pi/team/config.sh`) plus the independent `TEAM_PM_MODEL`; a brief's `category:` selects
> one, and ownership never follows model strength.

## Change process

1. Need a new directory? The PM updates this file (and references it in the brief).
2. Temporary borrowing (e.g. one package handled by another agent for a phase) must be marked **temporary** in the
   brief together with the hand-over condition.
| `openspec/specs/**` · `openspec/config.yaml` | PM | 规格与配置是账本的一部分；archive 仅获任务书逐个点名的 capability spec 临时写权，不含 config |
| `openspec/changes/<change>/**` | 该 change 当前阶段的 owner（任务书明授） | propose 归提案者；apply 归实现者；archive 由非实现者 worker 在自己的 worktree/task branch 执行，仅写任务书枚举的 change、归档目标与报告 |
